          "title": "Energy of a Yellow Photon",
          "problemStatement": "Calculate the energy of a photon of yellow light having wavelength $\\\\lambda = 600\\\\text{ nm}$ ($600 \\\\times 10^{-9}\\\\text{ m}$).",
          "stepByStepSolution": [
            "Step 1: Identify $\\\\lambda = 6.0 \\\\times 10^{-7}\\\\text{ m}$, $h = 6.626 \\\\times 10^{-34}\\\\text{ J}\\\\cdot\\\\text{s}$, $c = 3.0 \\\\times 10^8\\\\text{ m/s}$.",
            "Step 2: Apply formula: $E = \\\\frac{hc}{\\\\lambda} = \\\\frac{6.626 \\\\times 10^{-34} \\\\times 3.0 \\\\times 10^8}{6.0 \\\\times 10^{-7}} = 3.313 \\\\times 10^{-19}\\\\text{ J}$."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "E = 3.313 \\\\times 10^{-19}\\\\text{ J}",
